.TH scan 1 0.2.8 https://github.com/dbowm91/cargo-cleanme "General Commands Manual"
.SH NAME
scan \- Reconcile the machine read\-only: full with `\-\-all`, explicit with ROOT, routine inventory with `\-\-known`
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBscan\fR [\fB\-\-known\fR] [\fB\-a\fR|\fB\-\-all\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fIROOT\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Reconcile the machine read\-only: full with `\-\-all`, explicit with ROOT, routine inventory with `\-\-known`.
.PP
Exactly one scope selector is required. An `ArgGroup` expresses that rather than a per\-argument `required_unless_present_all`, because a positional ROOT does not satisfy `required_unless_present` in clap 4 — `scan /tmp` still demanded `\-\-all`. The group also makes the selectors mutually exclusive as a consequence of the same declaration, so the conflict rules cannot drift from the requiredness rules.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-known\fR
Routine read\-only inventory over the maintenance scope
.TP
\fB\-a\fR, \fB\-\-all\fR
Full machine reconciliation.

Required when no ROOT and no `\-\-known` is given: this is the only operation that may expire learned roots, and it walks the whole platform, so it is never one keystroke from the front door.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
[\fIROOT\fR]
Optional bounded root. Makes the scan Explicit and bypasses configured ignore/unignore filters
